From: relay12 contributors
Subject: [PATCH] d3d11on12: shim the _Maybenull_ SAL annotation

d3dkmddi.h (pulled in transitively through d3dkmthk.h and d3d10umddi.h)
annotates a DXGK_FLIPQUEUE_LOG_ENTRY* field with _Maybenull_. Nothing in
this pch's include chain brings in a definition for it before that struct
is parsed, so llvm-mingw rejects it as an unknown type name -- the same
gap __in and __nullterminated already hit and were shimmed for just above.

Defined empty, matching the existing shims: these SAL annotations carry
no codegen meaning, only static-analysis intent that this toolchain does
not consume.
---
diff --git a/include/pch.hpp b/include/pch.hpp
index d1843ee..eb8fe3c 100644
--- a/include/pch.hpp
+++ b/include/pch.hpp
@@ -37,6 +37,10 @@ WINADAPTER_IID(IDxbcConverter,
 #ifndef __nullterminated
 #define __nullterminated
 #endif
+
+#ifndef _Maybenull_
+#define _Maybenull_
+#endif
 
 #ifdef WIN32_LEAN_AND_MEAN
 // This defines NTSTATUS and other types that are needed for kernel headers
